  "scientific_caveats": [
    "Original published 2026 fruit-bat study already reported acoustic gaze direction anticipates turns; not re-discovered here.",
    "Only original Carollia files, no Rousettus numerical trials available in original public GitHub source.",
    "8 source biological bats, 30 trial files, 1632 eligible calls at 0.2sec are not 1632 independent bats.",
    "The primary estimand is continuous circular angular MAE at all quality-eligible calls, not original paper's turn-direction classification.",
    "The geometry+sonar model does not improve mean error over geometry alone, and both can be worse than zero-change baseline.",
    "Source file trial positions may be derived from acoustic call positions, so gaze vs track source errors could be shared.",
    "No actual echo confusion/masking manipulation in this original source, and no prey capture or long-term individual memories measured.",
    "The source bat bootstrap interval is descriptive for within-study 8 bats and not a population or cross-species guarantee.",
    "No hyperparameter or quality thresholds were tuned after opening results; three source horizons had been fixed."
  ]
